1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[English subtitles are available]

2
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:09,760
Ai-ting, eat up.

3
00:00:11,870 --> 00:00:14,600
Ai-yu, where did you go to play today?

4
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:18,870
Mom, Ai-ting was so brave today.

5
00:00:19,090 --> 00:00:20,940
If she hadn't protected me,

6
00:00:21,030 --> 00:00:24,590
I would've been captured
by that strange granny.

7
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:26,660
Strange granny?

8
00:00:27,450 --> 00:00:28,950
We were in the park this afternoon

9
00:00:29,030 --> 00:00:30,440
and met an old lady.

10
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:32,330
She kept wanting to talk to us.

11
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:34,230
She even hugged Ai-yu.

12
00:00:35,370 --> 00:00:38,980
Aside from that,
I don't remember seeing her before,

13
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,180
but she knew our names.

14
00:00:42,010 --> 00:00:43,860
Really?

15
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:45,970
I'm glad you were there.

16
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:50,720
Ai-yu, listen to me.

17
00:00:50,810 --> 00:00:52,480
The next time you go to play

18
00:00:52,570 --> 00:00:53,720
when I'm not around,

19
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:55,780
remember to stay close
to your sister, okay?

20
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:58,030
Dried bean curd.

21
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:02,560
Is it good?

22
00:01:02,870 --> 00:01:03,660
Right.

23
00:01:04,410 --> 00:01:08,370
I have gifts for you both.

24
00:01:09,510 --> 00:01:10,960
One for each of you.

25
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:14,440
Thank you, Mom.

26
00:01:14,750 --> 00:01:16,020
Don't mention it.

27
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:19,460
I have one too.

28
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:20,600
Who is this?

29
00:01:20,690 --> 00:01:21,740
It's me.

30
00:01:21,830 --> 00:01:22,360
You.

31
00:01:22,450 --> 00:01:23,200
Ai-ting.

32
00:01:23,990 --> 00:01:25,789
Where did you get this charm?

33
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:27,770
It's hideous, so change it.

34
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:30,450
Change it, Ai-yu.

35
00:01:35,650 --> 00:01:38,070
Let's eat first.
I'll help you change it later.

36
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:01,780
Do you have anything else to wash?

37
00:02:09,570 --> 00:02:10,630
No.

38
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:15,070
Thank you.

39
00:02:18,370 --> 00:02:19,290
I did your laundry.

40
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:21,320
You can change back
into your own clothes tomorrow.

41
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:27,480
That's the guest room.
You can use that one.

42
00:02:27,610 --> 00:02:29,540
It's okay. I can sleep here.

43
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:32,050
-Really?
-Yes.

44
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:37,460
Can I ask you something?

45
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:38,650
Sure.

46
00:02:50,579 --> 00:02:52,340
When I woke up this morning,

47
00:02:52,690 --> 00:02:54,050
I realized

48
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:56,430
that the ring you gave me was missing.

49
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:00,170
Plus, you said just now

50
00:03:00,250 --> 00:03:02,760
that you've lost most of your powers.

51
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:06,020
You can't see the Reflection of Time.

52
00:03:06,150 --> 00:03:08,220
You can't go wherever you want.

53
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:12,790
You even started to sweat and get hungry.

54
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:15,960
Does that mean

55
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:20,100
you are no longer a Kawas?

56
00:03:23,530 --> 00:03:24,370
I don't know.

57
00:03:28,110 --> 00:03:29,560
Did this happen

58
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,630
because of me?

59
00:03:40,730 --> 00:03:42,630
I summoned you today

60
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:45,750
because I have a lot of questions for you.

61
00:03:47,510 --> 00:03:48,920
I really want to know.

62
00:03:49,579 --> 00:03:51,380
What happened

63
00:03:51,780 --> 00:03:53,760
after I got into the car accident?

64
00:03:55,740 --> 00:03:57,230
Why am I still alive?

65
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:00,400
Why are you still here?

66
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:03,080
Also, after I passed out,

67
00:04:03,170 --> 00:04:05,200
I remember going somewhere...

68
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,080
That place is

69
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:07,090
Mapatayay, the Yin Yang Junction.

70
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:10,300
What?

71
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:13,780
It's the path

72
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:15,450
that your soul walked through
after the accident.

73
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:19,800
The path that my soul walked through?

74
00:04:24,420 --> 00:04:26,800
Does that path

75
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:29,220
lead to the afterlife?

76
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:33,050
If you had gone through that door,

77
00:04:33,530 --> 00:04:34,590
there would be no coming back.

78
00:04:36,170 --> 00:04:37,620
That's why I stopped you.

79
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:41,890
In order to get you out of there,

80
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:43,960
I...

81
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:46,110
Tien-ti!

82
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,350
Stop right there.

83
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:15,900
Why did you save me?

84
00:05:19,950 --> 00:05:21,530
I remember what you said.

85
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:23,910
There is no need to make choices

86
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:26,240
when it comes to Kakarayan's plans.

87
00:05:27,380 --> 00:05:29,800
It's meaningless even if I choose.

88
00:05:30,730 --> 00:05:32,270
If that's the case,

89
00:05:33,810 --> 00:05:36,050
why did you save me in the end?

90
00:05:39,570 --> 00:05:40,890
Can you

91
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:45,030
not erase my memories?

92
00:05:51,630 --> 00:05:53,920
[The important thing]

93
00:05:54,050 --> 00:05:55,370
[that I've been]

94
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:58,140
[trying hard to look for.]

95
00:06:10,020 --> 00:06:12,310
I'm your guardian angel.

96
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:15,390
I can only protect you

97
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:18,070
if you live.

98
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:28,150
I'm sorry.

99
00:06:28,890 --> 00:06:33,210
I didn't understand what you just said.

100
00:06:34,570 --> 00:06:35,450
Is it...

101
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:36,730
It means,

102
00:06:38,970 --> 00:06:40,600
"Would I be here

103
00:06:41,430 --> 00:06:42,440
if I knew why?"

104
00:07:28,990 --> 00:07:29,650
How was it?

105
00:07:30,090 --> 00:07:31,720
Did you get to see
your two adorable granddaughters?

106
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:39,250
You're not angry, are you?

107
00:07:40,130 --> 00:07:42,060
I let you stay here because you wanted to.

108
00:07:42,150 --> 00:07:43,250
What is there to be angry about?

109
00:07:43,340 --> 00:07:44,390
You didn't tell me

110
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:45,760
that they don't remember me anymore.

111
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:47,120
You also didn't tell me

112
00:07:47,210 --> 00:07:49,450
they've erased the memory of my existence.

113
00:07:50,990 --> 00:07:53,460
Sorry, it's my fault.

114
00:07:53,850 --> 00:07:54,780
I forgot to remind you.

115
00:07:54,909 --> 00:07:55,310
You...

116
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,450
But so what?

117
00:07:57,150 --> 00:07:59,180
Even if I told you
that they've forgotten about you

118
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:00,890
and are living a happy life,

119
00:08:01,420 --> 00:08:02,870
wouldn't you want to stay?

120
00:08:04,590 --> 00:08:05,600
I stayed

121
00:08:06,090 --> 00:08:07,050
because I was worried

122
00:08:07,190 --> 00:08:08,550
that they would be alone.

123
00:08:09,250 --> 00:08:11,010
Now, I see that they're doing well.

124
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,390
As long as they're doing well,

125
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,120
that's enough for me.

126
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:22,500
Excuse me.

127
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:24,300
No way.

128
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:26,810
That's not how you feel.

129
00:08:27,470 --> 00:08:29,890
As you know, I'm free to travel
through people's hearts.

130
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:31,430
I know what people are thinking.

131
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:33,539
I'm really worried about you,

132
00:08:34,110 --> 00:08:35,520
seeing how stubborn you are.

133
00:08:38,030 --> 00:08:38,690
Raka.

134
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:41,280
You're obviously thinking

135
00:08:41,809 --> 00:08:42,960
that it was that woman

136
00:08:43,039 --> 00:08:44,940
who had abandoned the girls,

137
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:46,830
so why right does she have
to come back now?

138
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:48,150
All this time,

139
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:50,260
you've been the one
who has loved and sacrificed for them.

140
00:08:50,390 --> 00:08:53,470
It's only right that you should be
the one looking after them.

141
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:54,040
Am I right?

142
00:08:57,960 --> 00:08:59,060
I don't think that way.

143
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:02,140
Why are you denying it?

144
00:09:02,230 --> 00:09:03,630
There's nothing wrong with that.

145
00:09:03,810 --> 00:09:05,530
I would think so too.

146
00:09:05,610 --> 00:09:06,890
Rather than being a Kawas

147
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,610
who's only blessed
but can't have anything,

148
00:09:08,690 --> 00:09:10,850
being a lowly and dirty grandma

149
00:09:10,980 --> 00:09:12,520
who gets to keep all her loved ones

150
00:09:12,610 --> 00:09:13,450
is better.

151
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:14,720
Right?

152
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:17,490
Kakarayan has arranged for their mom

153
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:18,590
to take care of them.

154
00:09:19,520 --> 00:09:21,150
That's a great blessing.

155
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:22,950
Why would I be unsatisfied?

156
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:23,920
Kakarayan offers

157
00:09:24,010 --> 00:09:25,410
the kind of run-of-the-mill blessing

158
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:27,000
that you don't have to pay a price for.

159
00:09:27,090 --> 00:09:28,450
But I'm offering a chance.

160
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:29,770
A chance where it will return

161
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:31,660
as much as what you put in.

162
00:09:35,580 --> 00:09:36,590
What chance?

163
00:09:38,750 --> 00:09:40,370
A chance to love them again.

164
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:44,020
A blessing doesn't come at a cost,

165
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:46,440
but it can be taken away at any moment.

166
00:09:46,530 --> 00:09:47,850
But a chance is not like that.

167
00:09:48,820 --> 00:09:50,140
Although it will cost you a little,

168
00:09:50,710 --> 00:09:53,570
you can hold it tight

169
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:55,770
and no one can take it away.

170
00:10:42,450 --> 00:10:43,330
['Orad.]

171
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:44,960
[Can you hear me?]

172
00:10:45,050 --> 00:10:46,900
[What I dreamt]

173
00:10:46,990 --> 00:10:47,910
['Orad.]

174
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:49,540
[will be all the path you take.]

175
00:10:49,630 --> 00:10:51,780
[Wake up.]

176
00:10:51,910 --> 00:10:54,160
['Orad.]

177
00:10:58,430 --> 00:10:59,570
Are you okay?

178
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:02,300
Did you have a nightmare?

179
00:11:04,850 --> 00:11:06,570
You looked like you were suffering.

180
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:07,970
I was trying to wake you up,

181
00:11:08,110 --> 00:11:09,160
but I couldn't.

182
00:11:11,050 --> 00:11:11,620
No way.

183
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:14,040
There's no way I had a nightmare.

184
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:16,330
The messenger of Kakarayan doesn't dream.

185
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:22,670
When did I fall asleep?

186
00:11:24,870 --> 00:11:26,500
You were sitting here.

187
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:28,210
I didn't want to disturb you.

188
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:31,510
When I got up to get some water,

189
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:34,810
I saw you were already asleep.

190
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:38,380
What about you? Why are you still up?

191
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:42,120
I was thinking about some things.

192
00:11:44,670 --> 00:11:46,380
It made me exhausted
the more I thought about it.

193
00:11:46,650 --> 00:11:50,390
And the more I thought about it,
the more awake I became.

194
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:53,030
What were you thinking about?

195
00:11:58,170 --> 00:11:59,320
A lot of things.

196
00:12:00,370 --> 00:12:01,470
For instance,

197
00:12:03,190 --> 00:12:05,610
ever since you showed up,

198
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:09,830
my lost memories started coming back.

199
00:12:10,630 --> 00:12:14,150
The things I couldn't remember before.

200
00:12:18,810 --> 00:12:20,090
Most importantly,

201
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:22,110
I've thought it through.

202
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:26,420
All these years,

203
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:29,720
I believed too much in spiritual stuff

204
00:12:29,850 --> 00:12:32,630
that people around me made fun of me
for being superstitious.

205
00:12:34,250 --> 00:12:35,220
It's your fault.

206
00:12:36,190 --> 00:12:37,290
It's my fault?

207
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:39,000
Yes.

208
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:41,690
Have you forgotten?

209
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:45,160
I almost died in the hospital
when I was little.

210
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:46,700
But you saved me.

211
00:12:46,970 --> 00:12:48,640
When I was in high school,

212
00:12:49,170 --> 00:12:50,930
I burned my hand during class.

213
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:53,350
You were the one
who made my injury disappear.

214
00:12:54,010 --> 00:12:57,000
There are many other miracles
of different magnitudes.

215
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,850
Even though you wiped out my memories

216
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:04,390
and made me forget you,

217
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:07,820
I never forgot

218
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:09,630
that you protected me.

219
00:13:14,070 --> 00:13:15,960
That's why

220
00:13:16,930 --> 00:13:18,560
I kept thinking

221
00:13:18,690 --> 00:13:20,230
that there had to be a god

222
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:23,570
that was secretly protecting me.

223
00:13:23,660 --> 00:13:25,510
Do you know what you've put me through?

224
00:13:26,570 --> 00:13:28,810
It's because I didn't know
which God it was.

225
00:13:29,250 --> 00:13:31,580
I'd rather be wrong than let it slip away.

226
00:13:31,670 --> 00:13:33,910
That's why I prayed to everything.

227
00:13:34,130 --> 00:13:35,410
Every time something happens,

228
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:36,690
I always say...

229
00:13:36,770 --> 00:13:37,830
Thank God.

230
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:48,260
But after I came to my senses,

231
00:13:48,390 --> 00:13:50,590
I realized

232
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:54,200
there's one more thing I can't figure out.

233
00:13:54,290 --> 00:13:55,170
What is it?

234
00:13:57,280 --> 00:13:58,110
Well,

235
00:13:59,870 --> 00:14:02,650
when you erased my memories
to make me forget you

236
00:14:03,350 --> 00:14:05,330
and quit being my guardian angel,

237
00:14:06,250 --> 00:14:08,100
I realized

238
00:14:08,850 --> 00:14:11,000
that my life didn't change that much.

239
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:13,340
I'm still very lucky.

240
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:19,100
Those little miracles
you brought to me in the past

241
00:14:19,630 --> 00:14:21,210
are still happening.

242
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:26,180
So I thought

243
00:14:27,810 --> 00:14:29,400
could it be

244
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:33,530
that you erased my memories
so I could forget you,

245
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:36,170
but you didn't forget about me?

246
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:42,460
You've been protecting me
in secret all this while.

247
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:48,450
Thank you.

248
00:14:51,750 --> 00:14:54,740
You're overthinking.
There's no such thing.

249
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:56,630
Okay.

250
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:59,270
Then why is it that every time I go
to the convenience store,

251
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:00,190
I always manage

252
00:15:00,330 --> 00:15:02,000
to buy my favorite salmon rice balls?

253
00:15:02,130 --> 00:15:04,510
It's because no one else wants
to eat those things.

254
00:15:04,590 --> 00:15:06,840
It has nothing to do with me.

255
00:15:06,970 --> 00:15:08,640
Why is it that every time
I pitched an idea,

256
00:15:08,730 --> 00:15:10,670
those clients who didn't like me

257
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:12,250
and complained about our high prices

258
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:13,170
always ended up

259
00:15:13,310 --> 00:15:15,290
signing with us in the end?

260
00:15:15,590 --> 00:15:16,830
They would even introduce
other customers to us.

261
00:15:16,910 --> 00:15:19,200
On top of that,
they would even specifically ask for me.

262
00:15:19,380 --> 00:15:21,450
That's because you're lucky.

263
00:15:21,530 --> 00:15:22,900
It has nothing to do with me.

264
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:28,000
No, there's more.

265
00:15:28,090 --> 00:15:29,810
I fell off my bike.

266
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:32,620
I even rolled on the ground several times,

267
00:15:32,710 --> 00:15:35,000
but I didn't have any wounds on my body.

268
00:15:35,090 --> 00:15:36,670
It must have been your doing.
Who else could it be?

269
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:38,740
It's because you're thick-skinned
and can take a beating.

270
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:39,970
It has nothing to do with me.

271
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:46,880
Here.

272
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:49,080
Come here.

273
00:15:49,160 --> 00:15:50,130
I don't believe you.

274
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:51,280
Let me go.

275
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:52,680
Don't be ridiculous.

276
00:15:53,610 --> 00:15:54,710
What are you doing?

277
00:15:57,300 --> 00:15:58,320
What about this?

278
00:16:01,620 --> 00:16:02,800
What on earth is this?

279
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:07,290
Greg Hsu's autographed poster.

280
00:16:07,380 --> 00:16:09,270
What does that have to do with me?

281
00:16:10,370 --> 00:16:11,690
Stop pretending.

282
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:14,820
You must have known.

283
00:16:15,650 --> 00:16:16,970
I'm Greg's Babe.

284
00:16:18,510 --> 00:16:19,480
Greg's Babe?

285
00:16:19,790 --> 00:16:21,680
I'm sure you had something to do with it.

286
00:16:21,770 --> 00:16:22,780
The deadline had passed

287
00:16:22,870 --> 00:16:24,270
when I went online

288
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:26,250
to try and win the lucky draw,

289
00:16:26,390 --> 00:16:28,190
but I still got it.

290
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:31,490
It had to be you. Who else could it be?

291
00:16:31,580 --> 00:16:34,310
Which God would do such a thing for me?

292
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:36,730
Let's say you fainted,
got into an accident, and burned yourself.

293
00:16:36,860 --> 00:16:38,970
If you want to hold me
responsible for that

294
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:40,820
and claim that I protected you,

295
00:16:40,910 --> 00:16:42,010
that's fine by me.

296
00:16:42,090 --> 00:16:44,380
But if you think I went out of the way

297
00:16:44,470 --> 00:16:45,970
to get this for you,

298
00:16:46,050 --> 00:16:48,870
-you really belittled your guardian angel.
-Hush!

299
00:16:49,660 --> 00:16:50,670
What on earth?

300
00:16:50,810 --> 00:16:54,590
This is an autographed poster
of my beloved Greg.

301
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:56,260
What on earth? You're being ridiculous!

302
00:16:56,350 --> 00:16:57,140
You're being ridiculous!

303
00:16:57,230 --> 00:16:58,290
You're being ridiculous!

304
00:16:59,430 --> 00:17:00,710
You can go back on your own tomorrow.

305
00:17:13,380 --> 00:17:15,140
What's this?

306
00:17:15,270 --> 00:17:17,030
Maybe it's food.

307
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:18,260
"Sanfeng"?

308
00:17:19,619 --> 00:17:22,310
It sounds pretty similar to "Shanfeng."

309
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:23,720
This is plagiarism.

310
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:25,339
Mom.

311
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:26,839
Sue it.

312
00:17:27,150 --> 00:17:28,690
Then we'll get paid.

313
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:30,980
"Sanfeng, shanfeng, sanfeng."

314
00:17:31,060 --> 00:17:32,650
Wait, don't move.

315
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:40,040
Could this be

316
00:17:40,130 --> 00:17:41,620
what I think

317
00:17:43,030 --> 00:17:44,040
it is?

318
00:17:53,190 --> 00:17:55,660
Thank God.

319
00:17:56,800 --> 00:18:00,320
Thank God!

320
00:18:01,860 --> 00:18:05,510
I'm so happy!

321
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,690
Is she Greg's Babe?

322
00:18:11,940 --> 00:18:13,920
Hsieh Tien-ti, you're unbelievable.

323
00:18:14,010 --> 00:18:15,410
It's just a poster.

324
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:17,970
This isn't just a poster.

325
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:24,210
Look, this was signed by my beloved Greg.

326
00:18:25,140 --> 00:18:27,120
I never thought

327
00:18:28,170 --> 00:18:30,860
I would be holding

328
00:18:30,950 --> 00:18:34,070
something he has touched before.

329
00:18:36,180 --> 00:18:38,690
I'm so lucky.

330
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:41,200
Thank you.

331
00:18:41,590 --> 00:18:45,820
Thank you. How did I get so lucky?

332
00:18:46,870 --> 00:18:51,230
Thank you. I'm so lucky.

333
00:18:56,730 --> 00:18:57,830
You're welcome.

334
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:04,910
Greg's Babe!

335
00:19:10,760 --> 00:19:12,660
This is your home?

336
00:19:13,620 --> 00:19:14,200
Yes.

337
00:19:14,590 --> 00:19:15,210
Are you sure?

338
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:19,480
Is this the house
you brought me to last time?

339
00:19:21,890 --> 00:19:22,550
I'm sure.

340
00:19:23,170 --> 00:19:23,920
Okay.

341
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:29,330
So where exactly is the house?

342
00:19:31,710 --> 00:19:33,550
If I knew,

343
00:19:33,770 --> 00:19:36,060
I wouldn't be standing here.

344
00:19:36,150 --> 00:19:38,480
There you go again
with that foreign language.

345
00:19:38,610 --> 00:19:39,670
Can you translate it?

346
00:19:41,210 --> 00:19:42,840
It means,

347
00:19:43,150 --> 00:19:44,110
"If I knew,

348
00:19:44,250 --> 00:19:45,170
I wouldn't be standing here."

349
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:49,480
That's completely different
from what you said last night.

350
00:19:53,530 --> 00:19:55,110
Why did we come to this school?

351
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:56,170
We're here to find a professor.

352
00:19:56,700 --> 00:19:57,710
Which professor?

353
00:19:58,810 --> 00:19:59,820
He's the only Kawas

354
00:19:59,910 --> 00:20:02,330
that has a chance to stay in this world.

355
00:20:02,900 --> 00:20:04,050
If he's still here,

356
00:20:04,350 --> 00:20:06,600
maybe he'll know what happened to me.

357
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:09,060
Please attend the professor's memorial.

358
00:20:07,830 --> 00:20:09,630
[Li Pu-hui]

359
00:20:09,810 --> 00:20:10,380
Memorial?

360
00:20:11,390 --> 00:20:12,400
Professor?

361
00:20:13,900 --> 00:20:17,860
[Li Pu-hui]

362
00:20:17,950 --> 00:20:25,030
[In memory: A debtor and gambler,
not a pioneer, a well-deserved death]

363
00:20:22,040 --> 00:20:25,080
I just spoke to some students
from the department.

364
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:26,880
They said

365
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:32,290
that your friend passed away
the night before yesterday.

366
00:20:32,950 --> 00:20:33,880
How did he die?

367
00:20:35,110 --> 00:20:39,420
I think it's stage four cancer.

368
00:20:39,510 --> 00:20:40,960
It was sudden.

369
00:20:42,590 --> 00:20:45,270
I bet it was his wife, Malusakadat's idea.

370
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:48,400
He's an attention-seeker.

371
00:20:48,700 --> 00:20:49,850
If they had to use the Comb of Memories

372
00:20:49,930 --> 00:20:52,710
to erase all the memories
of the people related to him,

373
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:54,250
I don't know how long that would take.

374
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:55,870
This will be easier.

375
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,850
They faked his death
to erase his existence.

376
00:21:01,150 --> 00:21:05,990
[In memory: A debtor and gambler,
not a pioneer, a well-deserved death]

377
00:21:08,770 --> 00:21:12,510
♫ Alone ♫

378
00:21:12,590 --> 00:21:15,630
Thank you.

379
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:18,970
Give her a big applause.

380
00:21:19,110 --> 00:21:21,610
Let's drink to our friend, Peggy.

381
00:21:21,750 --> 00:21:23,810
You sing so well. Here, have a drink.

382
00:21:23,950 --> 00:21:25,970
I already had a few drinks.

383
00:21:26,060 --> 00:21:28,650
You had a few? Why didn't I see it?

384
00:21:28,740 --> 00:21:30,060
Hold on, my phone is ringing.

385
00:21:30,190 --> 00:21:31,470
I need to take this call.

386
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:33,360
How long do I have to wait?

387
00:21:33,450 --> 00:21:35,690
Let's just drink by ourselves.

388
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:38,820
Mr. Wang, it has been a while.

389
00:21:38,900 --> 00:21:41,370
I'll talk to you later.

390
00:21:41,460 --> 00:21:42,560
Okay.

391
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:43,830
You can still play with me.

392
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:45,590
Okay, let's play a kissing game.

393
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:47,040
That's too fast.

394
00:21:57,910 --> 00:21:59,500
It's me.

395
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:03,190
I need you to pick up my kids.

396
00:22:04,340 --> 00:22:05,220
I can't.

397
00:22:05,300 --> 00:22:07,900
I'm busy because I'm going
to have dinner with Mr. Wang later.

398
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:11,070
I didn't want kids either.

399
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:13,090
Children are troublesome, okay?

400
00:22:13,530 --> 00:22:16,170
But I accidentally got pregnant.

401
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:20,090
I don't know who their dad is.

402
00:22:21,890 --> 00:22:24,350
Please help me pick them up.

403
00:22:27,080 --> 00:22:28,140
Thank you.

404
00:22:28,230 --> 00:22:30,250
I'll treat you to a meal next time.

405
00:22:30,870 --> 00:22:34,390
There are a lot of customers
waiting for me today.

406
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:36,010
Thank you.

407
00:22:46,090 --> 00:22:48,990
Toothbrush and toothpaste.

408
00:22:50,050 --> 00:22:51,940
I just remembered.

409
00:22:52,030 --> 00:22:53,440
When you were the messenger of Kakarayan,

410
00:22:53,570 --> 00:22:55,200
did you need to brush your teeth?

411
00:23:01,270 --> 00:23:02,590
Actually, I think

412
00:23:03,030 --> 00:23:05,540
there's no rush for you
to return to your old self.

413
00:23:06,810 --> 00:23:08,350
Didn't you say so before?

414
00:23:08,970 --> 00:23:10,950
As the messenger of Kakarayan,

415
00:23:11,040 --> 00:23:12,970
all you do is carry out

416
00:23:13,060 --> 00:23:15,520
what Kakarayan has shown you
in the Reflection of Time.

417
00:23:16,050 --> 00:23:17,550
Which means

418
00:23:18,300 --> 00:23:20,580
you don't even have the power to decide

419
00:23:20,670 --> 00:23:21,460
how you want to live.

420
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:22,520
Don't you think

421
00:23:22,610 --> 00:23:24,060
it's meaningless that way?

422
00:23:25,560 --> 00:23:26,300
Think about it.

423
00:23:26,390 --> 00:23:27,540
When I bought dinner for you last night,

424
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:29,910
you got to choose what you wanted to eat.

425
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,010
In the future,

426
00:23:31,140 --> 00:23:32,020
you can choose what...

427
00:23:32,110 --> 00:23:33,040
Are you done?

428
00:23:34,310 --> 00:23:34,800
Yes.

429
00:23:35,150 --> 00:23:37,390
It's true that I've lost my power
as the messenger.

430
00:23:38,270 --> 00:23:39,370
But don't forget.

431
00:23:39,720 --> 00:23:41,480
My time in this world

432
00:23:41,570 --> 00:23:44,520
is longer than anything you've ever seen.

433
00:23:45,050 --> 00:23:46,540
You're just a human

434
00:23:46,630 --> 00:23:47,950
who has lived on this earth
for around 20 years.

435
00:23:48,520 --> 00:23:49,750
Are you sure you want to teach me

436
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:51,380
about the meaning of life?

437
00:23:52,310 --> 00:23:53,540
Yes, you're right.

438
00:23:54,200 --> 00:23:55,870
Humans are indeed the species

439
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:57,410
with the most authority in this world.

440
00:23:58,160 --> 00:23:59,040
But look

441
00:23:59,130 --> 00:24:00,140
at what those self-righteous choices

442
00:24:00,230 --> 00:24:01,680
have done to the world.

443
00:24:02,120 --> 00:24:03,040
This is why

444
00:24:03,170 --> 00:24:04,930
Kakarayan took back all the blessings.

445
00:24:05,810 --> 00:24:08,190
Okay, don't be mad.

446
00:24:09,110 --> 00:24:10,040
I'm sorry.

447
00:24:12,280 --> 00:24:13,950
I just thought my words

448
00:24:14,090 --> 00:24:15,320
could make you feel better.

449
00:24:18,350 --> 00:24:21,520
Yes, there's no way a mere human like me

450
00:24:21,610 --> 00:24:23,630
could have known

451
00:24:24,650 --> 00:24:26,580
what mighty Kawas like you

452
00:24:26,670 --> 00:24:27,680
are thinking.

453
00:24:29,840 --> 00:24:31,030
I'll go take a look over there

454
00:24:31,380 --> 00:24:32,830
to see if I missed anything.

455
00:24:33,310 --> 00:24:34,280
You can look around by yourself.

456
00:24:42,200 --> 00:24:44,220
Aren't we supposed to have a nice talk?

457
00:24:44,580 --> 00:24:46,290
What a temper.

458
00:24:47,700 --> 00:24:49,990
Can't you see all these things
that I bought for you?

459
00:24:50,520 --> 00:24:52,940
[When the tap was turned on
at the hot spring area,]

460
00:24:53,020 --> 00:24:55,580
[instead of warm, healing spring water,]

461
00:24:55,660 --> 00:24:58,220
[only cold underground water flowed out.]

462
00:24:58,300 --> 00:25:00,940
[Even the unique smell of sulfur is gone.]

463
00:25:01,600 --> 00:25:02,970
[A beach in Kenting, Pingtung,]

464
00:25:01,870 --> 00:25:10,270
[Dolphin Bay Elegy.
Dozens of dolphins beached at Kenting]

465
00:25:03,100 --> 00:25:05,430
[that is normally crowded with tourists]

466
00:25:05,520 --> 00:25:06,660
[was littered
with the carcasses of dolphins]

467
00:25:06,750 --> 00:25:09,080
[for some unknown reason.]

468
00:25:09,220 --> 00:25:11,200
[Breaking news.]

469
00:25:11,280 --> 00:25:14,230
[According to a statement
from the Central Weather Bureau,]

470
00:25:14,320 --> 00:25:16,080
[a storm front that was expected to...]

471
00:25:16,210 --> 00:25:16,870
[The company warns]

472
00:25:16,960 --> 00:25:18,720
[that between them
and the natives of the land,]

473
00:25:18,850 --> 00:25:21,530
[the sincerity of coexistence
and cooperation has never changed.]

474
00:25:22,150 --> 00:25:23,510
[Yes, you're right.]

475
00:25:24,220 --> 00:25:25,980
[Humans are indeed the species]

476
00:25:26,070 --> 00:25:28,000
[with the most authority in this world.]

477
00:25:28,130 --> 00:25:29,150
[But look]

478
00:25:29,230 --> 00:25:30,070
[at what those self-righteous choices]

479
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:31,870
[have done to the world.]

480
00:25:52,510 --> 00:25:53,610
Toem?

481
00:26:09,180 --> 00:26:10,020
'Orad!

482
00:26:25,380 --> 00:26:26,080
No!

483
00:26:37,560 --> 00:26:38,800
[I only hurt her]

484
00:26:38,580 --> 00:27:07,610
[Next episode]

485
00:26:38,930 --> 00:26:41,170
[because I wanted to see
how you would react.]

486
00:26:41,260 --> 00:26:43,240
[But this time,
you did something different.]

487
00:26:43,330 --> 00:26:44,690
You've betrayed Kakarayan.

488
00:26:44,780 --> 00:26:46,140
[Maybe through you,]

489
00:26:46,280 --> 00:26:48,690
[we can make you the guide
by performing the Ceremony of Connection]

490
00:26:48,780 --> 00:26:52,130
so that I can reconnect with Kakarayan.

491
00:26:52,210 --> 00:26:54,590
[You must have somehow]

492
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:56,830
[shared your powers as Kawas with her.]

493
00:26:56,920 --> 00:26:57,800
[Am I right?]

494
00:26:57,890 --> 00:26:59,520
[I knew it.
You saw the Reflection of Time.]

495
00:27:00,180 --> 00:27:01,630
[Why would I do something]

496
00:27:01,720 --> 00:27:02,510
that probably

497
00:27:03,040 --> 00:27:03,870
and definitely

498
00:27:04,840 --> 00:27:06,380
[won't happen?]

499
00:27:16,110 --> 00:27:22,220
[2016, Stay with Me]

500
00:28:24,260 --> 00:28:25,010
Hi.

501
00:28:26,460 --> 00:28:27,120
What's wrong?

502
00:28:30,900 --> 00:28:32,570
I just had a nightmare.

503
00:28:33,540 --> 00:28:34,550
I haven't been able to sleep

504
00:28:34,640 --> 00:28:36,620
after waking up.

505
00:28:37,150 --> 00:28:38,820
I thought

506
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:42,170
I could find someone to talk to.

507
00:28:45,470 --> 00:28:46,870
Isn't someone there?

508
00:28:49,470 --> 00:28:53,030
She just broke up with her boyfriend,
so I feel bad for her.

509
00:28:53,170 --> 00:28:54,570
I don't want to wake her.

510
00:28:55,980 --> 00:28:57,480
So what can I do for you?

511
00:28:58,530 --> 00:28:59,410
Do you want me to chat with you?

512
00:29:01,570 --> 00:29:03,370
You have no idea about my ordeal.

513
00:29:03,460 --> 00:29:05,620
I've been having this nightmare for days.

514
00:29:05,750 --> 00:29:06,980
I can't sleep.

515
00:29:08,390 --> 00:29:10,850
I have to make my pitch
to Ms. Chang-fen tomorrow.

516
00:29:10,940 --> 00:29:12,920
If I can't sleep tonight,

517
00:29:13,710 --> 00:29:15,380
I'll really die.

518
00:29:17,100 --> 00:29:18,990
So you don't want to have nightmares?

519
00:29:22,380 --> 00:29:25,460
Then what do you want to dream about?

520
00:29:28,190 --> 00:29:30,040
As long as I can sleep through the night

521
00:29:31,620 --> 00:29:34,040
with a good dream,

522
00:29:34,440 --> 00:29:35,490
that would be great.

523
00:29:38,440 --> 00:29:39,360
That's easy.

524
00:29:42,180 --> 00:29:42,930
Can you do it?

525
00:29:43,190 --> 00:29:43,630
Here.

526
00:29:44,070 --> 00:29:45,080
Really?

527
00:29:51,730 --> 00:29:53,750
Hold on, let me get comfortable.

528
00:29:56,740 --> 00:29:57,400
Okay.

529
00:29:59,380 --> 00:30:00,610
Close your eyes.

530
00:30:13,110 --> 00:30:15,180
From now on,

531
00:30:16,230 --> 00:30:19,620
you're going to sleep like a baby.

532
00:30:20,990 --> 00:30:22,170
Tonight,

533
00:30:23,410 --> 00:30:24,770
you won't have the nightmare

534
00:30:24,900 --> 00:30:26,530
that has been haunting you.

535
00:30:27,500 --> 00:30:30,660
You'll be dreaming
of the moment in your memory

536
00:30:32,160 --> 00:30:36,120
that lets you feel the most relaxed,

537
00:30:37,260 --> 00:30:39,680
at ease, and untroubled.

538
00:30:43,030 --> 00:30:44,480
Maybe when you wake up,

539
00:30:44,570 --> 00:30:45,840
you'll forget what you've experienced

540
00:30:45,980 --> 00:30:47,250
in the dream.

541
00:30:48,660 --> 00:30:50,510
But this feeling of relief

542
00:30:51,170 --> 00:30:53,980
[will be with you every day
for the rest of your life.]
